From 9d99a611e1b3ba411b56c6dd9e11273f6a8dc269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:07:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0118 -- test hook to simulate a MISSED
 color_map hook

DOSAGS_DISABLE_COLORMAP_HOOK=1 deliberately does not install patch 0117's
lazy hook, so a blend reaches Allegro with color_map pointing at the
identity table instead of a real one.

This exists because patch 0117's safety property was untestable by any
other means. Once "table never built" is the common case, every consumer
path becomes one that has never executed in testing, and DOSBox-X cannot
catch a hook we missed because the path will not execute there either.
The failure mode is not a glitch: libsrc/allegro/src/c/cspr.h:545
dereferences color_map before the pixel loop and after the clip
early-outs, so without the identity table a missed hook is a hard fault on
real hardware.

Proven with the new bench8 `dark` scene, all three states:
  - table built eagerly and used:      PH01 7e0a277e3d4758c8 (reference)
  - table skipped, lazy hook fires:    PH01 7e0a277e3d4758c8 (IDENTICAL)
  - table skipped, hook MISSING:       PH01 94b0d885d8ebca78, exit_code=0

The third is the one that had never run. It renders instead of faulting,
and the degradation is confined to the blended sprite: the character draws
unblended at full colour rather than darkened. Cosmetic, localised, alive.
---
 Engine/ac/region.cpp | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Engine/ac/region.cpp b/Engine/ac/region.cpp
index 1d36d4de2..258b8601d 100644
--- a/Engine/ac/region.cpp
+++ b/Engine/ac/region.cpp
@@ -268,7 +268,19 @@ void generate_light_table()
     // blend entry points reach us through a function pointer rather than
     // a direct call. Installed here because this runs at every room load,
     // before any drawing can happen.
-    dos_port_ensure_color_map = &dos_port_build_light_table;
+    //
+    // DOS-PORT patch 0118, TEST HOOK: DOSAGS_DISABLE_COLORMAP_HOOK=1
+    // deliberately does NOT install it, to simulate a hook we missed.
+    //
+    // That is the case the identity table exists for, and the only way to
+    // exercise it: with the table skipped and no hook, a blend reaches
+    // Allegro with color_map pointing at the identity table instead of a
+    // real one. It must RENDER -- wrongly is fine -- rather than fault.
+    // libsrc/allegro/src/c/cspr.h:545 dereferences color_map before the
+    // pixel loop, so without the fallback this is a hard crash, and the
+    // point of the test is that it is not.
+    if (getenv("DOSAGS_DISABLE_COLORMAP_HOOK") == nullptr)
+        dos_port_ensure_color_map = &dos_port_build_light_table;
 
     dp_ensure_identity_table();
 
